{"schema":1,
"kind":"trace",
"id":"tally_blocks",
"source":"tally_blocks.py",
"code":"def main() -> None:\n    a = int(input())\n    b = int(input())\n    n = int(input())\n    need = [a, b]\n    used = [0, 0]\n    done = [0, 0]\n    for _ in range(n):\n        p = int(input()) - 1\n        m = int(input())\n        used[p] += m\n        if used[p] >= need[p]:\n            done[p] = 1\n    print(used, done)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program keeps, for two problems, the minutes spent so far and whether the problem's subtask has cleared. It reads the two costs and the number of blocks, then adds each block of minutes to its problem's total and marks the subtask cleared once the total reaches the cost, however many blocks that took.",
"presets":[
